{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows","id":1237246,"title":"[OOC][MtAw 2e] Smoke and Shadows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-20T13:32:10-07:00","id":1237246,"title":"[OOC][MtAw 2e] Smoke and Shadows","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Smoke and Shadows</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Campaign</span></b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>A Consilium recovering from years of war is rocked by unrest, dark temptations and an old sin coming back into the light.</i></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The city of East Bay has a checkered past. Situated on the American east coast it has a long history for American standards and its Awakened citizens have for most of it lived under the shadow of the Guardians of the Veil. Sixty years ago however a dangerous power vacuum opened the door for the Seers of the Throne and a long conflict resulted. After a particularly hot phase of the war that resulted in devastating losses on both sides, including the life of the previous Hierach, a tentative truce has been struck with the Seers and things have stabilized \u2013 on the surface. Tensions build as a generation that has known only war tries to cope with the idea of peace, evidence of left handed practices and other war crimes come to light and to top it all off whispers of an ancient boogeyman returned put fear into the hearts of the Awakened.</span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The City &amp; Consilium</span></b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">East Bay is a fictional city on the east coast of the united states. You can imagine it as a cross of New York, Chicago and Boston all rolled into one. It\u2019s a harbor city and a river (the Lorn) is flowing through the city, cutting it roughly in half.<br /> The Pentacle is represented through the Vinorium Consilium \u2013 nobody quite remembers where the name comes from anymore \u2013 one of the oldest Consilia in the new world. For a long time it has been dominated by the Guardians of the Veil, but in the last decades the Adamantine Arrow and Free Council have been the dominant orders as periods of warfare against the seers have dominated local events. A little bit less than a year ago a particularly bloody series of exchanges has weakened both the Pentacle and the Seers to the point that a truce was agreed upon. A young th\u00e9arch going by the name Phoenix initiated the negotiations and claimed the position of Hierach as much through popular support as by skills in the duel arcane. Now the Consilium stands divided by those who favor the peace and those who feel that now would be the time to drive the Seers from East Bay \u2013 whatever the cost.<br /> Due to the long wartime and the rather paranoid regime that preceded it the Cabal has become the cornerstone of Awakened life in East Bay, even more so than in other Consilia. Mages only trust a chosen few and for many that means only their Cabal. The locations of Sancta and Sympathetic Names are treated as serious secrets and the Rights Sanctuary and Crossing are treated very seriously indeed here. Outside ones Cabal the Orders offer a greater support network though through the constant warfare mages seldom gathered for Caucus and even more rarely for a full blown Consilium \u2013 too great were the risks. This lead to a fractured Consilium where every Mage only knew few others outside their Cabal. Only the Heralds and Councilors and a few other politically minded individuals have a broader overview of the Awakened population of the city. Now with Peace and an influx of new Mages seeking to claim a part of the rich supernatural landscape of East Port for themselves without the threat of war this might change, but for the moment Consilium is still fractured and paranoid \u2013 old habits die hard.<br /> Outside the Pentacle there is a strong presence of Seers. There are few Nameless as the war has not been kind to those who lacked the support of cabal and order. However few does not mean none and in the hard times many had to turn to unsavory sources of power for survival. A gamut of other supernatural critters of every kind also exists as one would expect for a major city, though most know better than to meddle in awakened affairs.</span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The Rules</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">I already warned you: There will be quite a few houserules. I\u2019ll post all of them here, but I can\u2019t make any guarantees that I will think of every particularity right off the bat \u2013 if I feel the need to make a new houseruling I will announce it in the IC threat in a spoiler and add it to this sections.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failures:</b> If a roll does produces ones and no die shows a six or higher it\u2019s a dramatic failure. You will still get a beat if you produce a dramatic failure in this way, but they can not happen outside of chance dice (and player choice).<br /> <br /> <b>Legacies:</b> Legacies are ancient wisdom passed on from luminous masters of the craft. Not any two-bit wizard can create their own. To create a new legacy a Mage must have a Gnosis of 6 aswell as have attained Mastery of both the primary and secondary Arcanum of the Legacy. To teach a Legacy you are a part of to another Mage you need to have unlocked the third Attainment of the Legacy.<br /> I tend to give Legacies more leeway than RAW in their Attainments. You can take a look at my homebrew (signature) for some examples, but a good way to eyeball it would be that I tend to allow legacy attainments to have another reach.<br /> Legacy Oblations give Mana in accordance with their grade of initiation into the legacy. Meaning you get Mana equal to the highest attainment unlocked, not equal to the dots in the primary Arcanum.<br /> Legacies come with a Rote skill of their own, in addition to those unlocked by orders (to a total of 4).<br /> <br /> <b>Homebrew:</b> I\u2019m open to homebrewed merits and utility attainments. If you want to take something like that I\u2019m certainly open to it, though I may tweak or veto stuff I\u2019m uncomfortable with for any reason. Additional utility attainments beyond the first unlocked by reaching the appropriate Arcanum level can be purchased with 1 (lesser) or 2 (greater) xp.<br /> <b>Arcane Experience:</b> Half of the price (round down) of purchasing another Arcanum or Gnosis dot must be paid in Arcane Experience. If you don\u2019t explore the magical side of things you won\u2019t develop your magical abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Training Arcana:</b> Arcana outside your Paths and Legacies ruling Arcana require a teacher to be increased, regardless of rating. Why derive ourselves of this storyhook?<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom:</b> Does not exist as a stat. The consequences of your actions are their own rewards. Paradox is contained with a Resolve + Composure roll (taking a -1 penalty for every Soul Stone you have created). The Mad still exist, they usually come to be when a Mage focusses on his or her obsessions to the exclusion of everything else.<br /> <br /> <b>Pattern Restoration:</b> Certain (supernatural) conditions cannot be removed using Pattern Restoration. An example would be things like a Vampire using Dominate on your character.<br /> Spirit Clash pools: Ephemeral Entities will use their Rank + Attribute for Clashes of Wills. This will make them quite more powerful in Clashes of Wills (as opposed to being ridiculously bad at it before, often rolling only their Rank as of RAW making even lesser Incarna pushovers for even Disciple mages), think twice about messing with Rank 3+ spirits, even if you are versed in the relevant Arcana.<br /> <br /> <b>Clashes of Wills and Mages:</b> First off you do not ALLWAYS know when one of your spells clashes another spell/ability. This is a case by case thing, but the most important example for this rule will be veiling spells. If somebody uses a veiling spell to hide a door and you cast a spell looking for hidden compartments then on a failure on the investigators part he will NOT be aware that he just ran into an illusion he failed to penetrate.<br /> <br /> <b>Enhancing Magic with Magic:</b><br /> Clashes of Wills: You can spend a wp to get the normal +3 dice and get the boni from duration and advanced potency, but otherwise the pool cannot further be enhanced by magic. No Prime/Fate Ruling or Perfecting spell can give you Potency dice or dice tricks on those.<br /> Spellcasting: Fate or Prime (or with some creativity maybe other Arcana) spells can give you dicetricks for spellcasting (9/8 again for ruling, Rote quality at Perfecting), but straight up dice boni are out of the picture.<br /> <br /> <b>Reflexive Spellcasting:</b> Will mostly not be a thing, looking at you there Exceptional Luck. I\u2019m fine with it in some cases, like the Death Veiling spells that lets you play dead, so feel free to ask. But I\u2019m going to say no in many cases.<br /> <br /> <b>Messing with Powerstats:</b> Is a no. You can\u2019t increase/decrease another Mages Gnosis by one with Prime Perfectign/Fraying, at least not really. Same for Spirit ranks, Blood Potency, whatever.<br /> <br /> <b>Surpassing the Dicecap:</b> Can usually be done with a Mana and a reach, I will take this option out. Not really because it\u2019s necessarily to powerful or anything, it just tends to lead to prolonged and completely unfun preparation fests (and forces me to consider NPCs doing the same which is a lot of really unimportant work I\u2019d rather not do, figuring out the spells npcs would have running is a chore already).<br /> <br /> <b>Specific Spells:</b><br /> Shifting Sands \u2013 The reach to travel back a whole scene can only be taken once.<br /> <br /> <b>Rotes:</b><br /> Using a rote for a spell of an Arcanum you have mastered grants another free reach.<br /> <br /> Sympathy:<br /> Not knowing the sympathetic name of the target will (in addition to increasing withstand) reduce the effective degree of sympathy by one, resulting in weak sympathy being unable to establish a connection at all if you do not know the targets name. </span><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Character Creation</b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">You start out as established mages. Wether you\u2019re a new arrival or a native, just finished your apprenticeship or have been around the block on your own for some time is up to you.<br /> Who is your character? What are her Aspirations, her Obsessions? What are your goals ooc (if any), what would you like to see/experience in this campaign? What are the Associates (Acolytes, Friends, Family, etc.) of your character? What\u2019s his or her history?<br /> Rules wise use the standard chargen for MtAw 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition with the following changes:<br /> Gnosis starts at two without any additional cost. You cannot trade in your starting Merit points for additional points of Gnosis.<br /> If you want to start initiated into a Legacy you can trade one merit point for a Legacy Attainment.</span> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Cast</span></b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\">@Second Chances</a></b> -<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> -<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> -<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a> -<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24231-gamora\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24231\" data-vbnamecard=\"24231\">gamora</a> -</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 07-26-2018, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T13:36:34-07:00","id":1237248,"title":"","content":"My character is being as a i type this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:04:32-07:00","id":1237255,"title":"","content":"Reserving this space for an eventual document link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:07:18-07:00","id":1237258,"title":"","content":"As I've pointed out before I'd appreciate it if you guys could brainstorm a little bit about what you want your cabal to be like. Maybe I'm just traumatized, but I've seen a number of expertly crafted characters utterly incapable of functioning together due to personality/goal differences a few too many times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:14:19-07:00","id":1237261,"title":"","content":"okay. My character is an Obssesive person. His name is Erik Angelo,Shadow Name Lumiel.<br /> He's a real life min-max. Has very little skills,but he is extremely badass on the ones he does have,he knows damn near everything there is to know about ghosts. He awakened at 14,he's 24 now and he spent 95% of his time studying magic. He neglected social situations,has very little friends,little connection to family. And he's onky realizing that now! So,one of his aspirations is to find a girlfriend,he' also good at making friends,he just never tried before. He's crazy good at the Egregore,a small high ranking member of the mysterium. He wants to be the top dog of the order one day,<br /> He also really bloody loves ghosts,he has empathy for their sadness,the horror of their existence,so he spends most of his time helping. Anything a ghost aks he does,he feels guilty is he doesnt.<br /> He's eager to make friends,join a cabal,find a girlfriend and help even more ghosts!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:17:16-07:00","id":1237265,"title":"","content":"I Also bought five dots at mentor,because his mentor is the baddest motherfucker in town,Lucifel gave Lumiel his Shadow Name. Lucifel is a Mastigos,who spends most of this time stealing banks to give money to the poor. He's a rogue,a crazy person but he loves Lumiel/Erik like a son. Lucifel is not part of any order but the mages all respect his power. He oftens helps Lumiel when he can,but aalmost always extract a price for his actions.<br /> He also,gave Lumiel his shadow name,When young erik said he want to be a light to lead ghosts into the afterlife,Lucifel told Erik about the angel of light,Lumiel. And that's the name he picked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:25:43-07:00","id":1237271,"title":"","content":"Just checking, Nicolas, is Erik a Moros?<br /> <br /> I had been leaning toward a Moros myself, but I also have Acanthus and Mastigos ideas I've been juggling. ... Also an Obrimos, now that I think of it. Welp~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 07-20-2018, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:32:13-07:00","id":1237275,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a> A few questions. Don't worry I think your ideas are groovy, I just tend to pick things apart and want to know a bit more about your character.<br /> So as an obsessive and for allmost all of his life (including formative years) downright antisocial person he is good and talented at making friends. How come? How does he deal with the anxiety talking to other people certainly would cause to such a person? Due to his background he seems to have had allmost no opportunity to develop social skills.<br /> Regarding Egregore I'm fine with you taking the merit, up to 5 if you really want it, but the initiations its taking its name from are part of a bigger mysterium social order a starting char would not have the qualifactions to go through (amongst other things starting chars just aren't magically proficient enough for anything past... the second initiation, I think?). But that's fine, more opportunities to undergo them later IC! Regarding your status in the order I think there are certain limits however. You can certainly have &quot;high&quot; order status, but I think high for a starting char would probably end at 3 and even then your character would need to have some extraordinary accomplishments and abilities under his belt.<br /> Incidentially the highest ranking Mystagogue in the area is leading a cabal focussed on studying the underworld and death, we'll have to figure out a reason why you are *not* a member of said cabal.<br /> His proclivity for helping ghosts will get you into all sorts of trouble, considering how unreasonable they can be. It will probably also be a point of derision for other mages aware of the habit, many mages have rather dim views of ghosts and their personhood (not saying they are right, mages just tend to be egomaniacal dicks and the world is easier when the ghost you enslaved isn't really a person for this or that reason).<br /> Regarding your mentor I'll have to think about it first - I have a certain power structure in mind and throwing in a random all powerful badass wildcard mage is not really going to be conductive to the campaign, so this is a tentative no. There are certainly mages who could function as a 5 dot mentor though.<br /> Morrigan, Mystagogue Councilor and leader of the Lords of the Below is for example a Master of Death and would be sufficiently powerful to serve as a five dot mentor. There is also another mage who could work for your char stat wise, but is really a militant isolationist, so I see no reason why he'd tutor your char.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> <br /> Don't be afraid to make a Moros just because someone else also does. We don't need to represent every Path and indeed having holes in the party often can lead to interesting storyhooks. A Path offers enough thematic material to support many different char concepts anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 07-20-2018, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:43:08-07:00","id":1237281,"title":"","content":"hmmm,can i rule Lumiel was actually a social person,just not with living people? Back when he awakened he started to see ghosts almost immediatelly,and they often talk to him The ghosts taught him everything he knows about the occult,he had several teachers from the Underworld.S,he's actually had a lot of scoail interaction,just not with the living. Does that sound good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:45:32-07:00","id":1237283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237281#post1237281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmm,can i rule Lumiel was actually a social person,just not with living people? Back when he awakened he started to see ghosts almost immediatelly,and they often talk to him The ghosts taught him everything he knows about the occult,he had several teachers from the Underworld.S,he's actually had a lot of scoail interaction,just not with the living. Does that sound good?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like it would cause even more of a disconnect when dealing with living people, really. Ghosts are not entirely like the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:46:35-07:00","id":1237284,"title":"","content":"If,you want tochange my mentor,that's fine. As long as he is pwoerful and resourcefoul enough to warrant five dots i'm okay with it.<br /> As for the reason he didn't join the underworld cabal,i'll rule that secretely,Erik/Lumiel is also an egocentirc guy,he doesn't want to be part of cabal studying the underworld ebcause he wants to be the greateast student of the underworld ever,and he doesnt want anyone helping him because he wants all the glory to himself. As a player,i want him to learn that it is bs in game,i want to go through the old trope of an arrogant person learning humility,painfully if needeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:49:13-07:00","id":1237285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237283#post1237283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like it would cause even more of a disconnect when dealing with living people, really. Ghosts are not entirely like the living.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man,can i just rule my character has a knack for social situations,that he just didnt want to put to use? I really would prefer no to change the dots on my sheet right now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:54:13-07:00","id":1237287,"title":"","content":"Well a five dot mentor would sure mean a Master - who I should mention are going to be rather rare in my Campaign. Mages knowledgeable about the Consilium (which many would not be) would likely know about three Masters in total in the whole Consilium (though there may be more who do not advertise their skill). Hence my reluctance to add another super powerful figure into the mix.<br /> <br /> For your char Morrigan seems like the most likely choice, we just have to work out why she'd take an interest in your char (there is allways a catch with mages ambitious enough to become so powerful...) and how your relationship is working out.<br /> <br /> Regarding your social dots: Dots on the sheet should follow the story of the char not the other way around. But I think we can twist this in a way that makes sense AND gives you what you want (I think?). Just say that he wasn't a complete recluse for all these years, instead he allways had had an easy way connecting to people on the surface - but he's never formed any deep bonds for one reason or another. All his relationships are shallow and he wants to change that now (though that brings up the question: why the sudden change of heart?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 07-20-2018, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:55:17-07:00","id":1237288,"title":"","content":"As for his status in the mysterium,he only has one dot on Status. but he has four dots on Egregore because he spend all his time studying and training magic instead of making connections and trying to ascend the ladder. He only realized how little of a player he is recently,and now he wants to advance on his status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:59:22-07:00","id":1237291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237287#post1237287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well a five dot mentor would sure mean a Master - who I should mention are going to be rather rare in my Campaign. Mages knowledgeable about the Consilium (which many would not be) would likely know about three Masters in total in the whole Consilium (though there may be more who do not advertise their skill). Hence my reluctance to add another super powerful figure into the mix.<br /> <br /> For your char Morrigan seems like the most likely choice, we just have to work out why she'd take an interest in your char (there is allways a catch with mages ambitious enough to become so powerful...) and how your relationship is working out.<br /> <br /> Regarding your social dots: Dots on the sheet should follow the story of the char not the other way around. But I think we can twist this in a way that makes sense AND gives you what you want (I think?). Just say that he wasn't a complete recluse for all these years, instead he allways had had an easy way connecting to people on the surface - but he's never formed any deep bonds for one reason or another. All his relationships are shallow and he wants to change that now (though that brings up the question: why the sudden change of heart?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh i know,he changed his heart because a ghost approached him one day. And that ghost didn't want any requests of him,didn't want anything too difficult. the ghost just wanted to be heard. When Erik/Lumiel heard the ghost story he realize how important other people really are. Furthermore once the ghost was done,he disapearead,not going back to the underworld but for what Lumiel firmly believes is Heaven","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:00:05-07:00","id":1237292,"title":"","content":"Sorry if i'm being difficult by the way,i'm kinda new to this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:01:33-07:00","id":1237294,"title":"","content":"Well, my Moros ideas are:<br /> 1. Death-focused Arrow who Awakened during the near-collapse of the Yakuza family for whom she worked. She goes digging for ghostly victims and uses what intel they can provide against the still-living people who victimized those ghosts. She'd still have ties to the diminished Yakuza, particularly to the boss.<br /> 2. Matter-focused Libertine electrician who came to East Bay to get away from the Triads; she found her Awakening in the patterns in her crocheting, the same patterns she saw in the street layouts, the wiring of houses, the cracks in the pavement.<br /> <br /> There's also my less-well-defined Obrimos, who at this point is a pharmaceutical chemist who managed drug production for a criminal organization---until they tried to kill her but only managed to give her nerve damage and boot her into a spiraling Awakening.<br /> <br /> (Also, Nicolas, it might be preferable to edit your additions into your posts instead of double- or triple-posting.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:02:43-07:00","id":1237296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237294#post1237294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my Moros ideas are:<br /> 1. Death-focused Arrow who Awakened during the near-collapse of the Yakuza family for whom she worked. She goes digging for ghostly victims and uses what intel they can provide against the still-living people who victimized those ghosts. She'd still have ties to the diminished Yakuza, particularly to the boss.<br /> 2. Matter-focused Libertine electrician who came to East Bay to get away from the Triads; she found her Awakening in the patterns in her crocheting, the same patterns she saw in the street layouts, the wiring of houses, the cracks in the pavement.<br /> <br /> There's also my less-well-defined Obrimos, who at this point is a pharmaceutical chemist who managed drug production for a criminal organization---until they tried to kill her but only managed to give her nerve damage and boot her into a spiraling Awakening.<br /> <br /> (Also, Nicolas, it might be preferable to edit your additions into your posts instead of double- or triple-posting.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right,i just think so fast sometimes i end up typing the &quot;post&quot; button before i'm done. i think you should go with option 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:07:28-07:00","id":1237299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237292#post1237292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if i'm being difficult by the way,i'm kinda new to this</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not being difficult, don't worry about it. I explicitly said I don't mind people new to the game joining. So far you're taking criticism well and that is a very valuable trait. The ghost inducing a change of heart is certainly possible. I take it, given his shadow name and this story, that your character is firmly christian?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> <br /> I can work with any of those, the first Moros is a classic and the second certainly sounds like it could lead to all kinds of weird augury! I think the most important part is that you play the character you are most interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:16:25-07:00","id":1237302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237299#post1237299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not being difficult, don't worry about it. I explicitly said I don't mind people new to the game joining. So far you're taking criticism well and that is a very valuable trait. The ghost inducing a change of heart is certainly possible. I take it, given his shadow name and this story, that your character is firmly christian?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a><br /> I can work with any of those, the first Moros is a classic and the second certainly sounds like it could lead to all kinds of weird augury! I think the most important part is that you play the character you are most interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes,he's praticant,goes to church and sometimes gets a little big headed at times,thinking what he saw in stygia means he specifically chosen by God to help ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:01:27-07:00","id":1237324,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking I'll go with the Matter Moros: Xionou, known to the mage world as \u200bQi\u0101n L\u00f3ng. She has 0 dots of Mentor, but the closest thing is Granny Lyons (an Acanthus Libertine, the wily old landlady of an apartment complex). Xionou lives in what is essentially East Bay's Chinatown and often does electrical work for a local Tong group, mostly because they have little love of the people she came here to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:13:09-07:00","id":1237328,"title":"","content":"Sweet! Am in the process of getting married, so it will take a few days for me to post anything, but I've got an idea brewing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:14:13-07:00","id":1237329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237302#post1237302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes,he's praticant,goes to church and sometimes gets a little big headed at times,thinking what he saw in stygia means he specifically chosen by God to help ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so you are aware: While religious Awakened definitly exist they face a certain bias due to the existence of the Father and his involvement with Sleeper religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237324#post1237324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking I'll go with the Matter Moros: Xionou, known to the mage world as \u200bQi\u0101n L\u00f3ng. She has 0 dots of Mentor, but the closest thing is Granny Lyons (an Acanthus Libertine, the wily old landlady of an apartment complex). Xionou lives in what is essentially East Bay's Chinatown and often does electrical work for a local Tong group, mostly because they have little love of the people she came here to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:22:50-07:00","id":1237331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237329#post1237329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just so you are aware: While religious Awakened definitly exist they face a certain bias due to the existence of the Father and his involvement with Sleeper religion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sounds good!</div> </div> </div> </div>understood :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:34:17-07:00","id":1237332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237328#post1237328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sweet! Am in the process of getting married, so it will take a few days for me to post anything, but I've got an idea brewing</div> </div> </div> </div>oh my god! i'm so happy for you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T00:08:37-07:00","id":1237426,"title":"","content":"Okay, I haven't read through the entire thread yet (been busy!), but here are some brief thoughts.<br /> <br /> The concept for my character is a zookeeper of the strange and bizarre. Basically a Mage who is intensely interested in the diversity of life, both natural and supernatural. Was a zookeeper prior to Awakening along the Thrysus Path and ended up joining the Mysterium. Primarily deals with Spirits and Ghost for now, but will likely pick up Mind in the future to deal with Goetia too. May also dabble in other places depending on what other supernatural shenanigans arise. Has a spirit familiar, may be tarantulas, may be hippo, may end up being some other animal.<br /> <br /> Int 3 Wits 3 Res 2<br /> Str 1 Dex 3 Sta 2<br /> Pre 3 Man 1 Com 3<br /> <br /> Death 2, Spirit 2, Life 1, Prime 1<br /> <br /> So it looks like I've give some Arcana, social, and Obsession links to both Nicolas' and Beans' characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T05:33:11-07:00","id":1237459,"title":"","content":"The Mysterium connection is interesting given some things I've decided about Xionou---namely, she's deeply concerned with Sleepers. Unsurprising given she's a Libertine, but it's also due to coming in early enough to see the tail end of last year's war, as well as having seen years and years of gang war in her native Hong Kong. Her platform is basically sane proto-Technocracy, in that she thinks protecting Sleepers from the fallout of supernatural conflict should be a priority. Given the Mysterium is the Order least concerned with Sleepers, she's likely to have some ideological disagreements with some of y'all guys' associates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T10:13:16-07:00","id":1237528,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> First off: congratulations!<br /> It's kind of ironic that the two predominantly Mysterium cabals I had set down before reading about the char ideas you guys had were the Lords of the Below on the one side (explorers of the mysteries of death, though specifically the underworld more than just Ghosts in general, all members styling themselves after gods of death) and Animal House on the other (a cabal that claims a national park close to the city as their territory and is amongst other things invested in studying local cryptids). At least you guys will have collegues... or competition.<br /> One thing that jumps out at me regarding your char is that as a zookeeper he probably had to do a decent amount of physical work, thus I'd expect his Strength to be a bit higher. Any reason for the low score IC?<br /> I allways approve of familiars!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> <br /> Is Xionous Shadow Name playing on the chinese emperor or something else? Iirc Tong can mean different kinds of chinese immigrant organizations, sometimes criminal. What kind of Tong were you envisioning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T10:52:15-07:00","id":1237537,"title":"","content":"Her Shadow Name, Qi\u0101n L\u00f3ng, is at least supposed to mean &quot;Pewter Dragon&quot; (which is, yes, a reference to the Technocracy's alternate name of &quot;Five Metal Dragons&quot;, because I am a dork). Admittedly I cobbled it together from several sites and Google Translate so it might be <i>all kinds of bogus</i>.<br /> As for the local Tongs, I figure they're not totally above-board, but their criminal activities are probably small-scale. Part of why she associates with them is because they don't like the Triads any more than she does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T14:05:36-07:00","id":1238051,"title":"","content":"... Did I poorly-translated-Chinese the thread to death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T14:28:36-07:00","id":1238058,"title":"","content":"Nono I should hope not. I just didn't have an immediate response/follow up question.<br /> <br /> I'm currently busying myself fleshing out some more important npcs, but as soon as everyone has their concept down I'd like to talk cabal/background with you guys.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24231-gamora\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24231\" data-vbnamecard=\"24231\">gamora</a> still interested/around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T17:35:16-07:00","id":1238092,"title":"","content":"Oh,sorry, I thought we'd continue the discussion on roll20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T02:32:22-07:00","id":1238161,"title":"","content":"No, I intend to use roll20 primarily for its dicerolling capabilities, unless someone is radically opposed to it. I might upload some other content there later, but the game itself will take place in an IC thread here on the forums. while OOC discussions will mostly take place here in this tread (or via skype if someone wants to run something past me quickly).<br /> <br /> One question for all of you: does somebody intent to start out holding any kind of special consilium or order position? (Like Herald, Sentinel, Provost even)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 07-24-2018, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T07:31:29-07:00","id":1238221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1238161#post1238161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I intend to use roll20 primarily for its dicerolling capabilities, unless someone is radically opposed to it. I might upload some other content there later, but the game itself will take place in an IC thread here on the forums. while OOC discussions will mostly take place here in this tread (or via skype if someone wants to run something past me quickly).<br /> <br /> One question for all of you: does somebody intent to start out holding any kind of special consilium or order position? (Like Herald, Sentinel, Provost even)</div> </div> </div> </div>personally,it wouldn't make sense for my character to have that,since he spent so much time in reclusion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T10:56:09-07:00","id":1238280,"title":"","content":"I don't think Xionou would have a special position either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:48:21-07:00","id":1238308,"title":"","content":"Mhhm I figured you two probably wouldn't, but I figured Arcanist might be interested given what I've heard about his char so far.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a> I've given it some more thought and narrowed down possibilities for a suitable mentor in setting for your character down to two possibilities.<br /> <br /> First would be the aforementioned Mystagogue, Morrigan. She'd certainly be able to help your char advance himself in the order aswell as mystically, seeing as she is one of the most potent mages in the consilium and specializing in the Death Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Second would be a more.... mysterious character. Frankly your character would probably not even directly know he HAS a mentor, but receive tutelage and guidance nevertheless, though in indirect ways.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> anything I should know about Granny Lyons/Xionous relationship with her? Any other notable people in her life, wether mundane or supernatural?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T12:14:35-07:00","id":1238319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1238308#post1238308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mhhm I figured you two probably wouldn't, but I figured Arcanist might be interested given what I've heard about his char so far.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a> I've given it some more thought and narrowed down possibilities for a suitable mentor in setting for your character down to two possibilities.<br /> <br /> First would be the aforementioned Mystagogue, Morrigan. She'd certainly be able to help your char advance himself in the order aswell as mystically, seeing as she is one of the most potent mages in the consilium and specializing in the Death Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Second would be a more.... mysterious character. Frankly your character would probably not even directly know he HAS a mentor, but receive tutelage and guidance nevertheless, though in indirect ways.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> anything I should know about Granny Lyons/Xionous relationship with her? Any other notable people in her life, wether mundane or supernatural?</div> </div> </div> </div>I Think i'll go with the the mysterious one then,just for the fun of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T12:30:34-07:00","id":1238326,"title":"","content":"Good, good... you can still ooc ask for specific &quot;favours&quot; as you normally could mechanically. They'll just take the form of happenstance IC and aren't actually voiced IC. Of course such a potent figure behind the scenes might arrange for things you didn't ask for coming along your way aswell!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T12:37:24-07:00","id":1238331,"title":"","content":"Granny Lyons is blind, kindly, and as wily as an Acanthus should be. She probably tends to call on Xionou when someone at the apartment complex she runs is in need of an electrician.<br /> <br /> I imagine another important person would be whoever runs the local Tong. If I had to give them a name, it'd probably be Tommy Keng. I imagine he'd be the sort of person who looks out for his own and prefers to keep serious crime out of his neighborhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T12:39:48-07:00","id":1238332,"title":"","content":"I imagine Tommy would be a sleeper?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T12:49:16-07:00","id":1238333,"title":"","content":"Yeah, most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T13:09:53-07:00","id":1238337,"title":"","content":"Ok, cool. I actually allready have at least one plot hook for the Tong in mind.<br /> <br /> Slight tangent: If you guys want to purchase non Supernal Relics with the Artifact background that's fine with me. Mages collect all kinds of supernatural stuff afterall. So what does that mean? Basically if you think it'd be cool if you character had a fetish (ala Werewolf) or a Memento (or even a Deathmask if you dare) that's cool with me. Or just a magical artifact that isn't supernal in nature, such as a cloak of levitation or whatever. Advantage of supernal artifacts is that they're usually more flexible (you can cast the spell on others, change around spellfactors etc), while a cloak of levitation would just... well levitate whoever is wearing it. No paradox though which is cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T02:10:13-07:00","id":1238534,"title":"","content":"No thanks, as ai said, too slow. You guys have fun though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24231-gamora","name":"gamora","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T07:17:22-07:00","id":1238576,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks for the heads up!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a> looks like you can join in afterall!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T12:04:28-07:00","id":1238646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1238326#post1238326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good, good... you can still ooc ask for specific &quot;favours&quot; as you normally could mechanically. They'll just take the form of happenstance IC and aren't actually voiced IC. Of course such a potent figure behind the scenes might arrange for things you didn't ask for coming along your way aswell!</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds amazing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T15:01:59-07:00","id":1238700,"title":"","content":"Alright, so I've talked over my character with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> and I'm ready to show her off now. <hr /><br /> Maya Abernathy is the daughter of Pakistani immigrants to the USA. Her mother was a professor of sociology, her father a respected lawyer. In America, her mother became a primary school teacher, and her father became an accountant. After high school, Maya ended up studying law, and was &quot;graduated&quot; after burning most of her professional bridges. One of her professors, Alexander Denovo, ran an absolutely brutal internship program, one that he supplemented with Mind magic and thorough satisfaction in controlling and denying the consent of his students (especially the women). Maya Awakened after a close friend of hers, fellow law student Daphne Muir, had a complete breakdown in Denovo's firm from a combination of natural deprivation and the use of the Mind Arcanum.<br /> <br /> After law school (but before involvement in the Awakened community) she worked at a coffeeshop and dispensed pro bono legal advice to friends and members of the community, but managed to just barely keep her head above water. That is, until she was picked up Elayne Kevarian, senior partner at Albrecht and Ao, known to the Awakened world as Kebechet. Maya, now operating with the Shadow Name Tara, was ushered into the Awakened world, joining the Silver Ladder and being employed as a junior partner of Albrecht and Ao before becoming initiated as a member of Elayne's (and Denovo's) Legacy, the Deathless Kings, known more commonly as the Craftsmen. Now, she advocates for the living, the dead, and the Awakened, trying to resolve conflicts in a non-adversarial manner, while studying how relationships, Sympathy, and obligations influence destiny, paying off her student loans, and trying to find a cure for Daphne (whose parents she still speaks to regularly). <hr /><br /> <b>Character Concept: </b>Idealistic Lawyer <b>Virtue: </b>Compassionate <b>Vice: </b>Hasty <b>\u200bObsession: </b>How does Sympathy impact Destiny?<br /> <br /> <b>Path:</b> Acanthus<b> Order:</b> Silver Ladder <b>Legacy: </b>Deathless Kings (Craftsmen)<br /> <br /> <b>Rote Skills: </b>Expression, Persuasion, Subterfuge, Academics<br /> <br /> <b>Nimbus:</b> Shadows and Starlight <b>Dedicated Tool: </b>A silver inlaid kirpan that belonged to her grandfather<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Settle a ghost's estate, pay off my Student Loans, find a cure for Daphne<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3 <b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <br /> <b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 4* <b>Health: </b>7 <b>Speed: </b>9 <b>Initiative: </b>7 <b>Willpower: </b>7/7<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills: </b>Academics 3<sup>+</sup> (Law), Investigation 1, Politics 2, Occult 2*<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Skills: </b>Athletics 1, Survival 1, Weaponry 2 (Knives)<br /> <br /> <b>Social Skills: </b>Empathy 3 (Obligations)<sup>Mystery Cult Initiation</sup>, Expression 3 (Appeals), Persuasion 3<sup>+</sup>, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis: </b>2 <b>Mana: </b>10/11 <b>Arcana: </b>Fate 2, Death 2, Time 2 <b>Praxes: </b>Divination, Exceptional Luck<br /> <br /> <b>Rotes: </b>Warding Gesture (Subterfuge), Postcognition (Academics), Shifting the Odds (Subterfuge)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Order Status (Silver Ladder) 1*, High Speech*, Mystery Cult Initiation 4 (Speciality in Obligations [Empathy], Pusher, Professional Training [Law: Persuasion and Academics. Contacts: Funeral Homes, DA's Office] 2, Mentor [Elayne Kevarian: Politics, Socialize, Resources] 3), Shadow Name 1, Fighting Finesse, Trained Observer 1<br /> <br /> Note: Two Merit dots sacrificed for Legacy Attainments<br /> <br /> *= Derived from Mage Template <sup>+</sup> = Asset Skills for Professional Training <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Deathless Kings (The Craftsmen)</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Originating in Eastern Europe at the end of the Reformation in the 17th Century, this Legacy was founded by a doctor of law known as Maester Gerhardt. He had many theories about the nature of the human soul, writing a treatise known as <i>Die Thaumas</i>, which posited that the nature of Sympathy, Destiny, magic, and even divinity, was that of systems in relationship with one another. Those who could learn the laws of that divine system could learn to manipulate them, and those with sufficiently powerful obligations could extend their lives well beyond a human lifetime, ending their lives only when they are good and ready and have planned a suitable afterlife, whether in the Underworld, using their own corpse, or even stranger means.<br /> <br /> Modern Craftsmen seek to continue Gerhardt's work, and also mediate between the living, the dead, the Awakened, and others, using their Attainments to forge enduring agreements between multiple parties. Ghosts and the mysteries of death and the Underworld are of particular interest to them, since ghosts seem to be defined by their obligations, their Anchors, and the things that they have left behind. By making and enforcing agreements and Oaths, they can bless the well-intentioned, punish the guilty, and maybe (just maybe) keep someone alive through their debts to others.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Acanthus, Silver Ladder, Seers of the Throne<br /> <b>Background: </b>The Deathless Kings draw from careers based in community and interpersonal relationships. Lawyers, social workers, educators, academics. Those who have built a web of obligations between themselves and others who feel the need to give back.<br /> <b>Appearance: </b>Craftsmen prefer to resemble professional mediators. Suits and the fashion favoured by professional academia are the order of the day, but whatever they need to look authoritative and in control is the order of the day.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Doctrine</span><br /> Prerequisites:</b> Death 2, Persuasion 2, and two dots of any of the following skills; Academics, Expression, Empathy, Investigation, Subterfuge<br /> <b>Initiation: </b>Prospective members of the Legacy are chosen by a mentor, hired for a single mediation &quot;case&quot;. The apprentice must perform to the standards of their mentor, resolving the case successfully and preferably in favour of their client. If they have performed to the satisfaction of their mentor, and can successfully defend themselves under the scrutiny of one or more senior members of the Legacy, then they have become a Craftsman.<br /> <b>Organization: </b>The Deathless Kings generally organize themselves into Mystery Cult &quot;firms&quot;, meant to professionally mediate and seek out potential students among the ranks of their interns, employees, and competition. Firms are run by senior students, and the most prestigious firms are run from the shadows by some of the original students of Gerhardt himself. They generally operate across an entire state or similarly sized region, senior partners travelling where they may, and having their pick of junior members to call to bring with them on assignment.<br /> <b>Theory: </b>Obligations and relationships tie us to the world, shape our personality, affect our lives and afterlives, and can even alter our Destinies. It is best, therefore, to cultivate advantageous relationships and enforce them through Oaths and Vows. Transactional relationships are the order of the day, and by taking control of them, you can take control of your place in the cosmos.<br /> <br /> Note: All Attainments of the Craftsmen can ignore Withstand if the target has broken an agreement with them, and reduces Withstand by one if the target is upholding an agreement with them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">First: Measure the Soul</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Initiation<br /> A Craftsman would be negligent to not check a prospective client (or their opposition) for the obligations that weight heaviest on them. This Attainment mimics the spell &quot;Soul Marks&quot; with Reach allocated to Instant casting and Sensory Range.<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Fate 1<br /> The Craftsman can expand their view of the web of agreements and connections in which their client (or opponent) sits at the centre. This Attainment mimics the spell &quot;Interconnections&quot; with Reach allocated to Instant casting and detecting possession, supernatural mind control, and alterations of destiny.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Second: Secure the Client</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Death 2, Persuasion 3<br /> Those most in need of a Craftsman's services are the dead, as they are those with the least say in their obligations, tied roughly to the unfinished business symbolized by their Anchors. This Attainment mimics the spell &quot;Speak with the Dead&quot; with Reach allocated to Instant use, Advanced Duration, and communicating with Rank 2+ Ghosts regardless of language.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Fate 2<br /> Having assessed the needs of a client, a Craftsman can draft an agreement. Over a scene of negotiation between the relevant parties involved in the process, the Craftsman at least ensures that they can know whether their mediation resulted in an agreement of good faith. This Attainment mimics the spell &quot;Oaths Fulfilled&quot;, with Reach allocated to Advanced Duration, seeing a brief vision of the fulfilled agreement, and tracking the subjects until the Duration elapses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 07-31-2018, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T16:10:02-07:00","id":1238711,"title":"","content":"Maya seems pretty cool! I haven't picked a Legacy yet, but I have two Merit dots I'm not really using and I'll probably work with Flinty to update or cobble together a good Legacy.<br /> Here's Xionou's <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Z1BJmIJFb7uiAazZvJfGrzv3E4t-wT_Y3WR18jhqX9E/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">WIP sheet.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:05:43-07:00","id":1238831,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> looks good! A few thoughts I had when looking over the stats: What does Eye for the Strange do again? I assume it's a two dot merit? You might get more mileage out of Presence than Manipulation given your profession (well both are extremly important to a lawyer) and specialties. But that depends alot on how you play her.<br /> We also should take another look at the second attainment, think we had worked out something slightly different, but it's slipping my mind for now, maybe I misremember. It's fine the way it is, but the withstand chicanery is missing so far, I think that'd tag onto the second attainment or at least part of it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> Looking forward to it, my first thought seeing your char legacy wise were the Transhuman Engineers, though I had only skimmed them so far, so I may be far off there!<br /> A few thoughts regarding your sheet so far: A weaponsmith should have at least passing familiarity with firing a gun. You don't have to be a sniper, but I recommend taking at leas a dot in Firearms. I'd think Crochet needles would be more weaponry than brawl, but if you want to keep your brawl we can treat them as a brawling weapon so to speak (probably a rather inefficient one unless you hit someone in the eye... or enhance them with a little magic!).<br /> Why the high Athletics? A three is afterall something many professional (if not top of their field) athletes would sport, why does she keep herself so active and agile and how?<br /> In her mentals: why does she have such &quot;high&quot; medicine? Usually people with an interest and some first aid experience would likely hav a 1 in it. I'm fine with it either way, just asking if there's a rationale in her background that explains the specific interest.<br /> In her socials I'd recommend a dot of streetwise given her affiliation with various less than legal organizations in both past and presence. Maybe move the dot from socialize there, since you stated your char to be rather quiet and unassuming, so it'd make sense for her to have no socialize in my mind.<br /> <br /> Regarding your backstory: Who was she apprentinced to? Granny Lyons, though sympathetic, is likely ill equipped to teach a young Moros, especially teaching you Forces would be likely beyond her. Did she teach you the basics and just outsource to various mages in the Assembly for magic lessons? Or did she have another teacher of her own path (can suggest a mage here if you want me to or make something up yourself).<br /> <br /> Did she take any active part in the pentacle/seer war or just tried to keep her head dow and not become a target? As a general aside the conflict wasn't limited to last year but has been a long lasting thign over the last half century (with hot and cold phases of course), last year was particularily bad. A whole bunch of cabals got destroyed and various fallout spilled over into the sleeper community (who generally interpreted it as gas leaks, race riots, terrorist attacks, freak illness and the like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T08:56:06-07:00","id":1238934,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> I switched my Presence and Manipulation scores around. Eye for the Strange lets you guarantee whether a particular event was supernatural or not, but now I'm thinking that's kind of useless given that the Awakened have Mage Sight. (And yes, it is a two dot Merit) I'll think of something else to spend those dots on. Will probably snag Fighting Finesse to make use of that Dexterity. The Withstand chicanery should probably be maintained throughout the Legacy. I'll edit it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T10:04:32-07:00","id":1238970,"title":"","content":"You might also want to take Alternate Identity, unless she uses her sympathetic name in her practice (which she well might, but your mentor probably would have pointed out to you how it makes you vulnerable on multiple levels).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:21:05-07:00","id":1238996,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I already have Shadow Name, doesn't that functionally do the same thing with the extra bonus of increased Withstand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T12:22:50-07:00","id":1239020,"title":"","content":"I meant more to protect your sympathetic name from your enemies.<br /> <br /> Guess that's a house rule I forgot to mention, in addition to the usual increase of withstand, not knowing the targets name will degrade the degree of sympathy by one (so weak connections cannot be used at all) making not knowing the sympathetic name a big deal again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T20:44:01-07:00","id":1239179,"title":"","content":"You'd be amazed how many things can delay a person from circling back to a thread. I've been roughly following along, but I may need to catch up on some of the details. I'll try to get a character sheet hammered out soon, but no promises, things keep cropping up. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237528#post1237528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> First off: congratulations!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! The day itself went super smoothly and was pretty much stress-free, which I was not expecting!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237528#post1237528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kind of ironic that the two predominantly Mysterium cabals I had set down before reading about the char ideas you guys had were the Lords of the Below on the one side (explorers of the mysteries of death, though specifically the underworld more than just Ghosts in general, all members styling themselves after gods of death) and Animal House on the other (a cabal that claims a national park close to the city as their territory and is amongst other things invested in studying local cryptids). At least you guys will have collegues... or competition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet! I love exploring the different types of creature in CofD, so that should be awesome!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237528#post1237528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that jumps out at me regarding your char is that as a zookeeper he probably had to do a decent amount of physical work, thus I'd expect his Strength to be a bit higher. Any reason for the low score IC?</div> </div> </div> </div>So question back at you... what gives you that impression?<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I was kinda using zookeeper as a short hand. I actually worked at a zoo and am basing my character (who really needs a name) off of a couple of friends. I don't think that strength is a prerequisite since staff at zoos tend to speciallize (so they have different requirements). Above and beyond that, physical confrontation with an animal means things have gone horribly, horribly wrong. I've given my character his Dexterity and Firearms to represent training with using tranq guns, which would be the actual method of resolution if things escalated. I'd also see Stamina as being more important to hauling things around all day than brute strength. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1237528#post1237528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I allways approve of familiars!</div> </div> </div> </div>Meeeee toooooooo! And since I had originally planned to trade some merit points for Gnosis, it looks like I now have enough to afford a four-dot familiar!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T23:33:33-07:00","id":1239204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1239179#post1239179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd be amazed how many things can delay a person from circling back to a thread. I've been roughly following along, but I may need to catch up on some of the details. I'll try to get a character sheet hammered out soon, but no promises, things keep cropping up.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1239179#post1239179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So question back at you... what gives you that impression?<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I was kinda using zookeeper as a short hand. I actually worked at a zoo and am basing my character (who really needs a name) off of a couple of friends. I don't think that strength is a prerequisite since staff at zoos tend to speciallize (so they have different requirements). Above and beyond that, physical confrontation with an animal means things have gone horribly, horribly wrong. I've given my character his Dexterity and Firearms to represent training with using tranq guns, which would be the actual method of resolution if things escalated. I'd also see Stamina as being more important to hauling things around all day than brute strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking mostly of hauling stuff around, like bags of food, where lift capacity does come into play. But hey I'll bow to your experience, it merely seemed to me like it'd involve a fair deal of lifting all in all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T23:51:07-07:00","id":1239209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1239204#post1239204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking mostly of hauling stuff around, like bags of food, where lift capacity does come into play. But hey I'll bow to your experience, it merely seemed to me like it'd involve a fair deal of lifting all in all.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. Forklifts and golf carts are wonderful things. Plus, we rarely give food to the animals straight, we'd rather make them work for it so that they get mental stimulation (aka enrichment). So rather than there being one big bundle of food to lift, we'll scatter it al, over the enclosure and make the animals go find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T01:42:01-07:00","id":1239225,"title":"","content":"Okay, cool!<br /> <br /> When writing up your characters backstory/sheet etc it'd be cool if you could give me an idea about the associates of your character (family/friends), any significant hobbies and anything else I could use as a plothook. Also even if you don't take the mentor merit it'd be cool to know who taught your character how to be a functioning mage (or a member of mage society anyhow). Aspirations and Obsessions are also prime storyhooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T06:15:23-07:00","id":1239270,"title":"","content":"<br /> Greetings all, late to the party but will aim to catch up quickly.<br /> <br /> I have skimmed the thread up to now but I am not 100% on the breakdown of characters we have so far. Is it 1 Acanthus, 2 Moros and a Thrysus? If that's the case I am probably going to look into making a Mastigos (I play an Obrimos already in another game.)<br /> <br /> I went with a Mastigos in the end, albeit one with a touch of Death about him. (Unfinished) Sheet here. <a href=\"https://www.myth-weavers.com/sheet.html#id=1654900\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.myth-weavers.com/sheet.html#id=1654900</a><br /> <br /> There is more detail regarding backstory in the sheet, but I will post the cliffnotes below.<br /> <br /> Veles was already in his 30's when he Awakened, but looking back he thinks he spent most of the previous 20 years trying to escape an inevitable trip to Hell. He certainly always seemed to be on the run from something. From an early age, he would hear voices no one else could, and occasionally glimpse horrors no one else could see. He soon learned to keep his uncanny observations to himself, struggling in school and becoming something of a loner.<br /> <br /> Perhaps as a result Martin has been mixed up in organised crime for most of his life, largely specialising in housebreaking, car-jacking and occasional drug smuggling. He Awakened and came to the Guardians attention at roughly the same time, when he was unwittingly hired by a Seer to steal a Grimoire from a Guardian storehouse. Against the odds he succeeded, and it was only when the old book started to to talk to him that things started to go sideways. The entity trapped inside the book tried to possess the thief, intent on devouring his soul and wearing his flesh like a new suit. In the midst of the spiritual confrontation, Martin made a commitment to never again run from his Demons and finally Awakened.<br /> <br /> Damascus, the Guardian in charge of the storehouse, tracked him down in time to retrieve the Grimoire and save the newly Awakened Martin. He took the man in, and taught him what he knew of Magic. <br /> <br /> Taking on the Shadow name Veles after the dark Slavic god of the underworld, Martin threw himself into his new life. His skills as a housebreaker now serve the guardians, and he has successfully retrieved all manner of relics and documents for the Order in the last few years. However he now finds himself in a strange place, a middle aged man with no real 'normal' life. He has few friends, no sleeper job, and lives in a rented one room flat. While his Obsession with magic is as strong as ever, he has made the conscious decision to try and build a more solid foundation for himself. After consulting with his Order colleagues, giving up the live of a Solitaire and petitioning to join a Cabal seems like a good first step. <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh PS: Just wanted to add that I had looked over the list of Homebrew rules hacks, and they all seem eminently sensible to me. I might look at stealing a few for the next time I run Mage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","user":"Katana1515","date":". 07-27-2018, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T07:02:12-07:00","id":1239291,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6230_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6230\" data-vbnamecard=\"6230\">Katana1515</a> <br /> Welcome abord!<br /> <br /> The current breakdown is:<br /> 1 Acanthus balancing Death, Fate and Time<br /> 1 Moros focussing on Matter with a dash of Forces<br /> 1 Moros presumably focussing on Death<br /> 1 Thyrsus balancing Spirit and Death, with a dash of Prime<br /> <br /> So far the group is very Death heavy. That said don't feel obligated to play a Mastigos just because the group doesn't have one, play whatever you want to play. If the group lacks certain Arcana between its members that's no problem, there are enough Mysteries out there (indeed there being a lack of information on some front can sometimes be rather beneficial to the story).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T07:21:48-07:00","id":1239298,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the breakdown! Ironically my original concept was a Bokor (another death focused Moros.) Maybe I should just give in and we can have something of a cabal theme?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T07:54:31-07:00","id":1239310,"title":"","content":"Sure, if that's what you want to play. Cabal Theme... well you guys will have to hash out what your cabal is like first!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T09:49:24-07:00","id":1239346,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, things have come up and I'm going to have to bow out. Sorry, team!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:58:29-07:00","id":1239525,"title":"","content":"Guys,i just had an idea. Since most of ours have Death,what if got together as a Cabal when an 7000 year ghost showed up and revealed us the location of a certain artifact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T00:26:04-07:00","id":1239586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1239525#post1239525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys,i just had an idea. Since most of ours have Death,what if got together as a Cabal when an 7000 year ghost showed up and revealed us the location of a certain artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thats a cool idea! I would definitely be on board with that, though 7000 years old might be a tad excessive <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, Unless Flinty has an idea for a Rank 8+ spectre to include in the Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","user":"Katana1515","date":". 07-28-2018, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T02:14:31-07:00","id":1239609,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> sorry to hear it, take care!<br /> <br /> Even a 7000 year old ghost is not necessarily Rank 6+ and if it was it wouldn't really be anything like the ghost of a real person anymore. It would likely be rank 4-5, which is really bad enough. The question with this idea is whom did a ghost reveal it to? Why did that person recruit the other chars of the cabal specifically. (And of course why and is it true at all etc. but that's for me to decide <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T05:52:13-07:00","id":1240400,"title":"","content":"So while you guys are building your character I thought I'd give you some more background info about some of the mages, cabals and structures of the Consilium your chars would likely know about.<br /> <br /> The Consilium has for security reasons compartmentalized information, thus your characters won't be aware of every mage or even cabal in the city, but here are some things your characters are aware of. <div align=\"center\"><b>Positions</b></div> <br /> <br /> Hierach &amp; Council - The Hierach, in theory, reigns supreme. In actuality he or she is dependant on the support of his or her councilors to keep her position. Thus the Council takes the place of advisors that cannot simply be ignored. Should a majority of the Council (3 or more) members vote to depose the current Hierach he or she must resign.<br /> <br /> Provosts - A sort of personal Herald for the individual Council members, the Provosts speak with the voice of their Councilor and handle most buisness for them, affording the Councilors themselves privacy and more importantly security. It's a highly heterogenous position. Due to the constant strife of the last decades the position has often been filled by less experienced members of the Consilium since more established members didn't want to take the risk. Provosts therefor vary vastly in their magical proficiency and status. A member in an order usually is aware of a contact protocol for their order's Provost.<br /> <br /> Sentinels - The Sentinels are the protectors of the Consilium and are entitled to commandeer any assistance wether personal or material from any mage of the consilium in line of their duty, as long as no member of the Council (or by extension their Provosts) says otherwise. There are currently two Sentinels, both Arrows, though the post has been known to be held by a Libertine in the past aswell. The current Sentinels are Benkei and Gallahad.<br /> <br /> Heralds - The Heralds are the lifeline of the Consilium. They are aware of the cabals of the consilium, their members and most of their sancta. In return every mage of the Consilium is aware of ways to contact every Herald. When one mage needs to get into contact with another they usually arrange a meeting via one of them. Because of the high amount of potentially disastrous information they posess every Herald is protected by several powerful protective spells (and restrictive Geas) laid upon them by the council and any attempt to subvert, influence or otherwise mess with the Heralds are summarily punished by death. Heralds usually serve for life and are forbidden from holding any other office for the duration of their term. Should one wish to retire they are required to undergo extensive memory manipulations. Aside from their main tasks each Herald also has special responsibilities such as representing the Concilium to outsders or looking out for specific groups of mages. <div align=\"center\"><b>Territory</b></div> <br /> <br /> The docks are disputed territory so to speak, both Seers and some Pentacle mages hold influence here. Tread lightly and don't tread in the water at all. Why? Because something is in there. You can go for a swim (whyever you'd want to) and likely come back in one piece, but mages and others exploring the depths of the bay often disappear.<br /> <br /> Downtown is Seer country, Mammon Pylons are deeply entrenched in the Skyscrapers of the financial district. Some Libertines try to contest it, but that's risky buisness. ESPECIALLY with the current truce. The Hierach has ordered Pentacle mages to give the area a wide berth.<br /> <br /> The Foxhall district is off limit to mages. An elusive cabal (The Black Vigil) has taken up residence there and placed a ban around the area barring other mages from entering. They are technically part of the Pentacle but they observe none of the rights and allmost never leave their claimed area. Anyone who makes it past the ban will be killed first and interrogated later. The last guy to try (12 years ago) ended as a particularily bloody spot on the sidewalk outside of Foxhall. Most are simply never seen again.<br /> <br /> Rushville National Park is a large, heavily forested area about 20 miles away from the city. Claimed by a local Cabal (Animal House) that only allows for crossing along certain paths. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Cabals</b></div> <br /> <br /> The New Dawn - The Hierachs cabal has made it its goal to usher in a new era of prosperit for the Consilium. It's a rather large cabal that only recently formed. Predominantly Silver Ladder and Adamantine Arrow, though all orders are represented.<br /> <br /> The Roundtable - The cabal of former Hierach Arthur. Arthur was an Adamantine Arrow and a master of the second degree. He held the title for more than 20 years (quite impressive given the dangers involved) before he died about a year ago. Most of his cabal died in the fighting with him, the remnants keep largely to themselves, though Gallahad holds the position of Sentinel and deputizes his cabalmates frequently. All members of the cabal are Adamantine Arrows and many belong to a Legacy called &quot;Knights of Avalon&quot;, said to have been founded by Arthur a decade ago. Arthus was said to posess a powerful artifact in the form of a sword, what has become of it nobody knows.<br /> <br /> The Swords of Liberty - Alongside the Roundtable the largest and most notorious warcabal in East Bay. They have weathered the storm relativly well and are not happy with the truce. Predominantly Free Council and Arrow, their leader is an experienced Libertine by the name of Theomacha.<br /> <br /> The Black Vigil - elusive, militaristic isolationist cabal that holds Foxhall. Many silently question wether their enormous secrecy is supposed to cover left handed practices.<br /> <br /> The Web - predominantly Libertine cabal dedicated to connecting the awakened and spreading information. They have multiple ties to other consilia and cabals near and far.<br /> <br /> The Melting Pot - After the fierce battles last year many cabals were shattered and since then there has been an influx of new mages in the consilium. The Melting Pot is a cabal founded to give these disenfranchised mages a (temporary) home. It has only a few permanent core members, but refugees and transients are welcome to use communal sancta and hallows until they move on or join a cabal of their own.<br /> <br /> Known to Tara (and other SL members): The Wise Ones - Predominantly Silver Ladder cabal whose members style themselves after Wise Men (or Women) from history (and myth) and try to guide the lives of sleepers towards awakening. Responsible for most Cryptopoly in East Bay. Cabal of the Silver Ladder Councilor Balthazar and his Provost Ptolemy.<br /> <br /> Know to Lumiel (and other Mysterium characters, so likely Second Chances' char): The Lords of the Below - A cabal that studies the mysteries of death and specifically of the underworld. Predominantly Mysterium and the keepers of the local Athenaeum. Predominantly Mysterium, the Councilor, her Provost and both Curators are members of this cabal. It's members all styled their shadow names about gods and spirits associated with death.<br /> <br /> Know to Lumiel (and other Mysterium characters, so likely Second Chances' char): Animal House - The second important Mysterium cabal, though less so than the Lords Below. They have claimed Rushville National Park, about 20 miles from the city, as their territory and allow crossing only along certain paths. Thyrsus heavy, invested in Spirit magics. Their members style their names after animals. <div align=\"center\"><b>Mages</b></div> <br /> <br /> Phoenix - The new Hierach. Very young for her position (or so it is said, she looks somewhere between 20 and 30, but due to magic that doesn't mean much) and very talented for her age. Came to East Bay merely five years ago but has gained great respect among the Arrow, Free Council and Ladder in this short time. Didn't ascend to the Hierachy uncontested, but strengthened her claim with the Duel Arcane (she appears to be a brilliant duelist). Far from being a pacifist she fought on the frontlines, but believes it's important to clean house and rebuild before fighting the seers. If both sides destroy each other completly the only ones winning are the Exarchs. She's Obrimos and a Th\u00e9arch.<br /> <br /> Hope - A young Obrimos who only finished her apprenticeship 2 years ago. Phoenix' student and now her Provost. Member of the New Dawn and a Th\u00e9arch.<br /> <br /> Benkei - A large and ugly fellow with a propensity for swordmanship. Member of the New Dawn, Adamantine Arrow and one of the Consiliums Sentinels.<br /> <br /> Theomacha - Longtime strategos of the local Assembly and therefore also Councilor for the Free Council, though recently some voices wonder wether the two positions should be decoupled. It's said that if any mage managed to make a personal enemy of the Father, it's her. Fiercly opposed to the Seers of the Throne and the Ministry of Paternoster in particular, she leads the Swords of Liberty and is one of the most vocal proponents for continued warfare. She was a longtime friend of the former Hierach, Arthur, and is one of the few Masters in the Consilium.<br /> <br /> Gaia - A matronly Th\u00e9arch who was instrumental in the founding of the Melting Pot. Has connections and allways an open ear for mages new to the Consilium. Member of the Melting Pot.<br /> <br /> Victoria - Fashionable and Elitist, the Th\u00e9arch is one of the Consilium's Heralds and tasked with handling external relationships - meaning non-Pentacle mages and other supernatural beings. Member of the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> Link - Libertine with a profound love for the digital age (and the movie Matrix). One of the Consilium's Heralds and tasked with handling relationships with other Consilia near and far. Member of the Web.<br /> <br /> Muse - Jovial Libertine who loves art. One of the Consilium's Heralds and tasked with welcoming and advising mages new to the Consilium.<br /> <br /> Gallahad - Erstwhile Provost of Arthur, now Sentinel of the Consilium. Adamantine Arrow and Member of the Roundtable.<br /> <br /> Known to Tara (and other SL chars): Balthazar - Elderly black gentleman, Obrimos, Thrice-Great, Master of Spirit, Deacon and Councilor for the Silver Ladder. Used to treat Phoenix as a rising star but their relationship has cooled considerably since she took the Hierachy he deemed his by right and humiliated him in the Duel Arcane. The local caucus is now split between Phoenix and Balthazar causing a fair deal of internal tension. Most prominent member of the Wise Ones.<br /> <br /> Known to Tara (and other SL chars): Ptolemy - Student and Provost to Balthazar, the aging Obrimos is the first point of contact for all buisness cocerning the local ladder. Member of the Wise Ones.<br /> <br /> Known to Mysterium chars: Morrigan - Moros, Hierophant and Councilor of the Mysterium. She is a Master of Death and member of the Lords of the Below. She, like the rest of the order, shows little interest in politics but in general the Caucus is in favour of peace as it stops fighting from interfering with their work.<br /> <br /> Known to Mysterium chars: Banshee - A rather morose woman dressing in funeral wear most of the time. Provost to the more elusive Morrigan and first point of contact for any Mysterium buisness. Member of the Lords of the Below.<br /> <br /> Known to Mysterium chars: Hades - An allmost skeletal, old man that still carries himself with suprising regality. One of the Curators of the local Athenaeum and member of the Lords of the Below.<br /> <br /> Known to Mysterium chars: Hecate - A rather strange woman with shifting appearance and personality. One of the Curators of the local Athenaeum and member of the Lords of the Below.<br /> <br /> These lists are of course far from complete, I've only detailed important people that you would likely know of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:59:52-07:00","id":1240435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1237246-ooc-mtaw-2e-smoke-and-shadows?p=1239609#post1239609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> sorry to hear it, take care!<br /> <br /> Even a 7000 year old ghost is not necessarily Rank 6+ and if it was it wouldn't really be anything like the ghost of a real person anymore. It would likely be rank 4-5, which is really bad enough. The question with this idea is whom did a ghost reveal it to? Why did that person recruit the other chars of the cabal specifically. (And of course why and is it true at all etc. but that's for me to decide <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay,i've come up with this: So the ghost had an struck of luck,he found an extremely potent artifact,an sarira! The ghost,who learned quite a bit about mages in his 7000 years of existence, is astonished that no mage has managed to find it but he knows most of them would do a lot for it. So he finds a group of mages at that might be interested,he decidess this cabal can be as good as any other,he tells them the location of the Sarira,but he begs them to do one thing for him first. He once watched a mage create a new ghost from scratch,just straight up creating a ghost is a spell almost all masters of death know. So the ghost begs the cabal to intercede with a Master for him. Why? The ghost wants a girlfriend,simple as that,he's lonely. he wants a mage to create a new ghost to be his eternal companion,once he has his girlfriend he'll tell the coterie about the Ruby Mistress<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Sarira</b></u><br /> <br /> There was once a a People who lived on what today is known as Ireland. A young woman of this People worshipped the Tuatha de Danaan,the Gods. and gave them all honors,she believed they would care for her . But her family was killed by a druid of great magical strenght. His magic,he claimed,was a gift of the Gods. He left the woman alive to suffer the loss, one day later she awakened,she tought of nothing but revenge.She spent the next 50 years growing more powerful,until she found her ancient enemy and destroyed him. But her thirst for blood wasn't sated,the man claimed the Gods have Gifted him,and where those gods might be if not in the Supernal? (It wasn't called the Supernal in ancient ireland,but i don't know which name they would use). So she vowed to Ascend,and to destroy the gods and take their place as ruler of the universe. No one knows if she suceeded,no one knows if the Gods were real. But the Supernal <i>is </i>real and she <i>did </i>Ascend. Her ascension left a Sarira,a statue of petite woman made almost entirely of wood,but with deep cruel eyes made of ruby. The ghost tells all that to the cabal. I don't know what the others will think but Lumiel realizes he did heard of some people who destroyed Gods and took those Gods places as rulers of the Universe,those people are called by the greek word for &quot;ruler from the outside&quot; Exarch. Others would be terrified,but Lumiel? The Arrogant little shit decided finding the Sarira was the first step on a long journey to destroy the Exarchs,especially that false God the Father.<br /> <br /> &quot;<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.tumblr.com/post/156083167600/sariras-relics-of-ascension-mage-the-awakening\" target=\"_blank\">Here's rules for making a Sarira</a><br /> <br /> Sounds good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:21:51-07:00","id":1240444,"title":"","content":"Well a few things. Before we get into specific plothooks I'd like to know how you guys became a cabal in the first place and what your reason for sticking together is. Simple protection, some common goal, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Plotwise I allready have a few things in mind I'll spring at you. I don't mind doing a general artifact hunt at some point (not sure I want to place it at the beginning, though) and what you suggest works in principle (allthough I'd change a few details of the story around).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":